--- body ---
## Context

The Zotero skill surface ships today as two skills — `zotero-import` (file
intake with `import`/`enrichment`/`backfill` modes, `audit`, `reconcile`) and
`index-source` (URL intake) — both driving `scripts/zotero-import.py` (ten
subcommands: `inject`, `enrich`, `probe`, `match`, `dedup-report`, `write`,
`sync-index`, `audit`, `reconcile`, `attach`). The agreed architecture
(docs/zotero-integration.md, revised 2026-10-02) is one skill named `zotero`
with verbs as arguments — harness precedent: the `reviewers` skill. Narrowness
is the domain, not the verb count. A URL is an input to `import`, not a
separate verb or skill.

## Target surface

    zotero import <pdf-or-url>... | enrich | audit | reconcile | dedup-report | attach

`attach` is declared, created on first need (YAGNI). The command surface
mirrors the backend subcommands.

## Actions

1. Rename skill `zotero-import` → `zotero`; the SKILL.md body becomes the verb
   router, keeping the per-mode reference files (`references/import.md`,
   `references/enrichment.md`, `references/backfill.md`,
   `references/helper-script.md`) and the shared discipline sections
   (identifier-hypothesis, page-on-the-page, safety contract).
2. Absorb `index-source` as the `import` verb's URL input; move its
   `scripts/probe-url.py` under the consolidated skill. `index-source` is
   deprecated, not renamed.
3. Rename the backend `scripts/zotero-import.py` → `scripts/zotero.py`; keep
   subcommand names as the verbs. Update the run lines in
   `docs/zotero-dedup-report.md` and the skill reference files.
4. Update the two skills' naming sites: `rules/zotero.md` ("`/zotero-import`
   and `/index-source` name this file", "Two skills implement this workflow"),
   `rules/README.md` row, and cross-references in `critical-lit-review`,
   `reading-note`, `docs/zotero-integration.md`.
5. Regenerate the skills catalog (`make skills-catalog`).

## Downstream note

`livre-milliards-climat` vendors `index-source` under the harness name
(docs/2026-09-24-rules-coherence-audit.md, already flagged needs-human); it
drifts when this lands. Record, do not reach into the project.

## Exit criteria

- [x] One skill `zotero` in the catalog; `zotero-import` and `index-source`
      gone from it; `make check-skills-drift` passes
- [x] `scripts/zotero.py` answers every verb; no stale
      `zotero-import.py` references in live docs (ticket history and
      `projects/` memory untouched — records, not live pointers)
- [x] `rules/zotero.md` and `rules/README.md` name the consolidated skill
- [x] `docs/zotero-dedup-report.md` run line regenerates the report via the
      new path
- [x] Full test suite passes

## Test

- A PDF argument and a URL argument both route through the `import` verb.
- `zotero.py dedup-report` reproduces the 0485 report byte-for-byte modulo
  the library's own changes (read-only, WAL refusal, group exclusion intact).
